BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:transmediale-festival-curation-2028@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260925T223601Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: transmediale 2028: Open Call for Festival Curation
DESCRIPTION:transmediale e.V. invites applications for the Festival Curatio
 n of transmediale 2028\, the Berlin festival for art and digital culture n
 ow in its 40th year. Since 2025 transmediale appoints a new curator for ea
 ch edition\, each bringing their own positionality on the present moment i
 n art and technology\; the organisation is especially interested in curato
 rial approaches that bring genuinely new questions and reference points to
  the field\, grounded in critical reflection and political engagement rath
 er than following technological trends. THE ROLE: develop the curatorial c
 oncept and full programme for transmediale 2028 (last week of January 2028
 )\, spanning a discourse programme (lectures\, panels\, conversations\, pr
 esentations\, talks)\, a workshop programme\, a video and film programme\,
  a performance programme\, and art projects presented during the festival 
 days\, plus events from longstanding and new partnerships. The curator wor
 ks closely with the festival team\, represents the festival publicly\, pla
 ys an active role in fundraising\, and contributes to transmediale's local
  and international networks. TASKS: establishing the festival concept\, th
 eme and title\; developing the event and programme structure with festival
  management and the executive and advisory board\; selecting participants\
 , projects and artworks\; producing related texts and contributing to publ
 ic relations and fundraising\; adhering to budget management policies and 
 helping acquire additional financial resources\; collaborating with the te
 am and submitting reports throughout. REQUIREMENTS: comprehensive knowledg
 e of international contemporary and media art with the ability to critical
 ly examine the intersection of art\, technology\, media\, science\, societ
 y and politics\; a clear curatorial and thematic vision\; at least 5 years
  of experience in programme development across multiple formats with an ex
 perimental approach (experience leading cultural projects is advantageous)
 \; solid fundraising experience for cultural and artistic projects\; a sup
 ra-regional network in the art and cultural scenes\; excellent communicati
 on skills\, integrity and a collaborative mindset\; fluency in English or 
 German\; alignment with transmediale's values. CONDITIONS: freelance posit
 ion\, December 2026 until March 2028\, ca. 70% commitment across the contr
 act period and full-time from October 2027\; Berlin-based or willing to re
 locate for key periods\, with relocation to Berlin required from October/N
 ovember 2027\; the position may be filled by an individual or a group. A c
 ontract extension for the 2029 edition will be considered in summer 2027. 
 SUBMISSION: application form (downloadable from the call page) plus a cove
 r letter of under 700 words\, via the submission platform only\; additiona
 l documents are not reviewed. Queries to apply[at]transmediale.de. Deadlin
 e 30 September 2026\, 23:59 CET.\n\nOrganisation: transmediale e.V.\nLocat
 ion: Berlin\, Germany. Berlin-based or willing to relocate for key periods
 \; relocation to Berlin is required from October/November 2027. Open inter
 nationally\; applicants must be fluent in English or German with at least 
 a good command of English.\nAward: EUR 40\,000 net for an individual or EU
 R 50\,000 net for a group\, as a freelance contract covering December 2026
  to March 2028 (ca. 70% commitment overall\, full-time from October 2027).
  Possible contract extension for the 2029 edition\, decided by the Advisor
 y and Executive Board in summer 2027. No application fee.\nDuration: Contr
 act December 2026 until March 2028\; the festival takes place in the last 
 week of January 2028\n\nMore: https://transmediale.de/en/news/open-call-fo
 r-festival-curation-2028?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=
 referral
URL:https://transmediale.de/en/news/open-call-for-festival-curation-2028?ut
 m_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Berlin\, Germany. Berlin-based or willing to relocate for key peri
 ods\; relocation to Berlin is required from October/November 2027. Open in
 ternationally\; applicants must be fluent in English or German with at lea
 st a good command of English.
END:VEVENT
